00:12:58,286 --> 00:13:12,036
如果我们要求一个前沿模型去估算一个项目的开发成本，比如我想构建一个可以在本地运行、
带有 AI 敌人的 3D 第一人称射击游戏。
If we ask a frontier model to estimate the development cost of a project, let's say I
want to build a 3D first person shooting game that I can play locally with AI enemies.

152
00:13:12,718 --> 00:13:15,268
你觉得这需要多长时间？
How long do you think that will take?

153
00:13:16,334 --> 00:13:17,924
让我们看看 Claude 会怎么说。
Let's see what Claude will say.

154
00:13:18,638 --> 00:13:19,492
好，出来了。
Okay, here it is.

155
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:22,884
你看，估算的时间是以天、周和月为单位的。
See the estimate is in days and weeks and months.

156
00:13:23,662 --> 00:13:30,788
但如果我们现在要求智能体去实际构建它，我敢保证它只需几分钟就能给出一个可运行的版本。
But if we ask the agent to actually build it now, I can guarantee it will come back with a playable version in just a few minutes.

157
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:33,060
因为我已经这样做很多次了。
Because I have done this so many times.

158
00:13:33,646 --> 00:13:38,404
这种不匹配是因为模型是基于人类数据训练出来的。
This mismatch is happening because the models were trained from human data.

159
00:13:38,766 --> 00:13:42,724
而这就是一个典型的开发者给出的估算。
And that is what a typical human developer would give as the estimate.

160
00:13:43,438 --> 00:13:46,852
AI 似乎还不知道它写代码的速度比人类快得多。
AI doesn't seem to know it can code much faster than humans yet.

161
00:13:47,214 --> 00:13:56,580
所以当 AI 在做技术决策时，它在隐性假设某些选项的开发成本比实际情况高得多。
So when AI is making technical decisions, it's implicitly assuming the
development cost for some of the options are much higher than they actually are.

162
00:13:57,134 --> 00:14:04,452
这会导致模型倾向于选择廉价的方案，而这些方案往往质量低、不可扩展或者难以维护。
This biases the model to choose cheap solutions that are often low quality, not scalable, or hard to maintain.

163
00:14:05,166 --> 00:14:07,972
所以我在这里制定了这个规则来纠正这种偏差。
So I have this rule here to correct that bias.

164
00:14:09,326 --> 00:14:21,280
我还规定在修复 Bug 时，始终先在端到端环境下重现 Bug，且要尽可能贴近最终用户的体验。
I also said when doing bug fixes, always start with reproducing the bug in an end-to-end
setting as closely aligned with how an end user would experience it as possible.

165
00:14:21,518 --> 00:14:29,956
现在的 AI 模型默认喜欢写单元测试，但这些往往不足以覆盖我们想要保护的产品行为。
AI models today, by default, like to write unit tests, which are often not
sufficient and not really covering the product behaviors we want to guard.

166
00:14:30,574 --> 00:14:34,160
